Z||000000||cowans||09-13-2000||03:04 PM||||Batboy,or Anyone else!!! I just read an archive on wiring after-market gauges. archive page 46..."wiring for aftermarket gauges". I'm installing a V8 with Autometer Phantom gauges in an F40. I am trying to find as much info as I can to set this up before I re-install the cradle. Any info appreciated, thanks, Sandy||||reg||1
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||09-13-2000||06:02 PM||||If its any help, I'm doing the same this winter.  I just got my speedo/tach, and I'm waiting on the rest of the gauges to put in the aux pod.  I talked to Batboy about his hookup before I bought, and from talking to him, it didn't seem that bad.  The only thing I was worried about was the speedo, and he said it wasn't that bad.  Tell me how it goes when you get it all together.<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||cowans||09-18-2000||08:36 AM||||Thanks BBBADGT. I just mounted the cradle, V8 and tranny back in this W/E. I was hoping someone might confirm my wiring colors for the gauges, ignition, etc. Posting to try again! Good luck, here's a pic of my F40.<P> - Mvc-001f.jpg||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||09-18-2000||06:29 PM||||Sandy,<P>FYI, if you are using an aftermarket water temp gauge, you will not be able to use the Fiero's sensor for the analog part.  <P>When I put in VDO gauges in my 308 kit, I still had the 2.8 V6 and I had to change out that sensor (losing the temp light but I did gain a better analog temp gauge.)<P>Also, the electronic speedo was fun ... I found that I had to use the Fiero's speedo's circuit board so that I could send the proper signal to the ECM and so that my cruise control got the right signal (remember, I was still running the stock engine/transaxle!)<P>If you are using a carb setup, you can just use the output from the VSS directly to the electronic speedo.  If you want to use the stock Fiero's cruise, then you will have to use the Fiero's speedo's circuit board.<P>If you are using TPI, I hoping that the Fiero's VSS will supply the needed signal for the ECM and from the ECM, you can hook up the electronic speedo without a problem.<P>Paul<BR><p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 09-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||cowans||09-19-2000||09:20 AM||||Thanks Paul, I was wondering about the speedo board. Yes, it is a carbed SBC.I was thinking I might run 2 sensors to retain the idiot light(temp), Sandy||||reg||7
Z||000005||batboy||09-20-2000||05:15 PM||||I'm bringing this post back to the top so I'll see it when I get home tonight. I might have some of those wiring color codes wrote down. I did not install any aftermarket gauges other than the speedo and tach. Sounds like Paul Herder gave you some good advice. I used a Auto Meter Sport Comp electronic speedo and the wiring hook-up was easy. I'm using a carbed engine with no cruise, so it was a simple matter of using the existing factory speed sensor (VSS) and then calibrating the speedo afterwards.||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||09-20-2000||11:08 PM||||Wiring code for the speedo connector that plugs into the bottom of the cluster.<P>P--black/white---ground<BR>R--purple/white--speedo<BR>S--yellow--------speed sensor<BR>T--yellow/black--12v switched<BR>U--brown---------cruise||||reg||1
Z||000007||cowans||09-21-2000||03:07 PM||||Thanks Batboy, If you have any other wiring to setup a carbed V8, send it along. I've toned out most of my wires, eg: oil press,etc.but always willing to double-check. Sandy||||reg||7
